      "url": "https://api.mathkangaroo.ca/api/v1/media/2013/2013gr0910e.pdf"
    },
    "grade": "9-10",
    "points": 3,
    "timeMinutes": null,
    "type": "mc",
    "prompt": "The eight semicircles built inside the square are congruent and the side of this square has length 4. What is the area of the non-shadowed part of the square?",
    "image": "qimages/kangaroo/ca-2013-g0910/q02.webp",
    "choices": [
      {
        "key": "A",
        "text": "$2\\pi$"
      },
      {
        "key": "B",
        "text": "8"
      },
      {
        "key": "C",
        "text": "$6+\\pi$"
      },
      {
        "key": "D",
        "text": "$3\\pi-2$"
      },
      {
        "key": "E",
        "text": "$3\\pi$"
      }
    ],
    "answer": "B",
    "acceptedAnswers": null,
    "answerUnit": null,
    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Semicircles minus overlaps",
        "body": "Each side carries two semicircles of diameter 2 (radius 1). In the picture a region is grey when it is covered by exactly one semicircle; where two semicircles overlap (the lens at each corner) it is white again.\n\n- Total area of the semicircles: $8 \\cdot \\frac{\\pi}{2} = 4\\pi$.\n- At a corner, the two semicircles centred at distance 1 from the corner overlap in a lens made of two quarter-circle segments: $2\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{4} - \\frac12\\right) = \\frac{\\pi}{2} - 1$. Four corners: $2\\pi - 4$.\n\nGrey area $=$ (sum of semicircles) $- 2 \\times$ (overlaps) $= 4\\pi - 2(2\\pi - 4) = 8$.\n\nWhite area $= 16 - 8 = 8$.\n\n**Answer: (B) 8**"
      },
      {
        "title": "White = centre + lenses",
        "body": "The white part consists of the central region (outside all semicircles) and the four white lenses at the corners.\n\n- The union of the semicircles has area (sum) $-$ (overlaps) $= 4\\pi - (2\\pi - 4) = 2\\pi + 4$, using the lens area $\\frac{\\pi}{2} - 1$ from the first solution. So the central region has area $16 - (2\\pi + 4) = 12 - 2\\pi$.\n- The four lenses have area $2\\pi - 4$.\n\nWhite area: $(12 - 2\\pi) + (2\\pi - 4) = 8$ — the $\\pi$'s cancel.\n\n**Answer: (B)**"
      }
    ],
    "topics": [
      "geometry"
    ],
    "difficulty": 1,
    "duplicateOf": null,
    "reviewNote": null
