    "type": "mc",
    "prompt": "The plan of the Scotts' family apartment is made in scale 1 : 50 and has a rectangular shape with dimensions 20 cm by 30 cm. What is the area of the apartment?",
    "image": null,
    "choices": [
      {
        "key": "A",
        "text": "12 m²"
      },
      {
        "key": "B",
        "text": "150 m²"
      },
      {
        "key": "C",
        "text": "300 m²"
      },
      {
        "key": "D",
        "text": "450 m²"
      },
      {
        "key": "E",
        "text": "600 m²"
      }
    ],
    "answer": "B",
    "acceptedAnswers": null,
    "answerUnit": null,
    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Scale the lengths",
        "body": "1 cm on the plan is 50 cm in reality. So the apartment measures $20 \\cdot 50 = 1000$ cm $= 10$ m by $30 \\cdot 50 = 1500$ cm $= 15$ m. Its area is $10 \\cdot 15 = 150$ m².\n\n**Answer: (B) 150 m²**"
      },
      {
        "title": "Scale the area",
        "body": "Areas scale with the square of the scale: the plan area $600$ cm² becomes $600 \\cdot 50^2 = 1\\,500\\,000$ cm² $= 150$ m² (since $1$ m² $= 10\\,000$ cm²).\n\n**Answer: (B)**"
      }
    ],
