    "type": "mc",
    "prompt": "In the picture the areas of the triangles are 5 and 10, as shown, and the lines a, b and c are parallel. If the distance between the lines a and c is 6, what is the length of PQ?",
    "image": "qimages/kangaroo/ca-2013-g0910/q17.webp",
    "choices": [
      {
        "key": "A",
        "text": "4"
      },
      {
        "key": "B",
        "text": "5"
      },
      {
        "key": "C",
        "text": "6"
      },
      {
        "key": "D",
        "text": "$\\frac{36}{5}$"
      },
      {
        "key": "E",
        "text": "$\\frac{15}{2}$"
      }
    ],
    "answer": "B",
    "acceptedAnswers": null,
    "answerUnit": null,
    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Common base PQ",
        "body": "Both triangles have the base $PQ$ on line $b$. The big triangle has its third vertex on $a$, so its height is the distance $h_1$ between $a$ and $b$; the small one has its third vertex on $c$, height $h_2$ = distance between $b$ and $c$.\n\n$$\\tfrac12 PQ\\cdot h_1 = 10, \\qquad \\tfrac12 PQ \\cdot h_2 = 5.$$\nAdding: $\\frac12 PQ (h_1 + h_2) = 15$, and $h_1 + h_2 = 6$, so $3\\, PQ = 15$ and $PQ = 5$.\n\n**Answer: (B) 5**"
      },
      {
        "title": "Ratio of heights",
        "body": "Same base, so the areas are in the ratio of the heights: $h_1 : h_2 = 10 : 5 = 2 : 1$. With $h_1 + h_2 = 6$: $h_1 = 4$, $h_2 = 2$. Then $\\frac12 \\cdot PQ \\cdot 4 = 10$ gives $PQ = 5$.\n\n**Answer: (B)**"
      }
    ],
