    "answerUnit": null,
    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Factor the vertex sum",
        "body": "Let the pairs of opposite faces carry $a, a'$; $b, b'$; $c, c'$. Every vertex touches exactly one face from each pair, and each choice of one face from each pair gives exactly one vertex. So the sum of the 8 vertex products is\n$$(a + a')(b + b')(c + c') = 1001 = 7 \\cdot 11 \\cdot 13.$$\nEach bracket is at least 2, so the three brackets must be 7, 11 and 13 in some order (1001 has no other factorisation into three factors $\\ge 2$). The sum of the face numbers is $7 + 11 + 13 = 31$.\n\n**Answer: (E) 31**"
      }
    ],
